---
description: Reconcile linked customer failures, authorized remedies, external operations and partial closure.
args:{request:RecoveryRequest;serviceState:ServiceRecoverySnapshot;prior?:ServiceRecoveryCheckpoint|null}
returns:ServiceRecoveryRun
---
Bind saved = prior when supplied, otherwise null. Bind scope = `frameServiceRecovery(request, serviceState.cases)` and policy = `selectRecoveryPolicy(serviceState.policyEditions, request.orderIds)`. Preserve case version, order scope and channel preference. Bind issues = `decomposeServiceIssues(scope, policy, serviceState.cases, serviceState.customerTimeline)`. Split only independently resolvable failures; keep earlier promises linked where later timing changes their value.

Bind entitlements = `resolveIssueEntitlements(scope, policy, issues.accepted, serviceState.orderAndPurchaseRecords, serviceState.documentedExceptions)`. Apply purchase-date edition and exact exception scope per issue. Keep mandatory entitlements distinct from discretionary gestures, and ask only for decisive missing evidence. Bind remedies = `buildJointRecoveryBundles(scope, policy, issues.accepted, entitlements.accepted, serviceState.paymentAndStockLedger, serviceState.customerChoices)`. Check amount limits, mutually exclusive remedies and duplicate compensation while preserving separately entitled issue outcomes.

Before promising scarce stock, require a current reservation and customer choice. Bind actions = `coordinateRecoveryOperations(scope, policy, remedies.accepted, serviceState.operationReceipts)`. Each action has a stable operation ID and matching authorization; if an external response is lost, read the receipt ledger first. Unknown effects are never retried blindly. Bind closure = `compareIssueClosure(scope, policy, issues.accepted, actions.accepted, serviceState.operationReceipts, serviceState.customerChoices)`. Close only issues with exact fulfillment receipts or explicit accepted alternatives.
Bind proposal: ServiceRecoveryProposal = { caseId: request.caseId, version: serviceState.version, issues, entitlements, remedies, actions, closure, uncertainOperations: action IDs without known outcome, expiredReservations: expired reservation IDs, partialOutcomes: partially completed issue IDs, pendingCustomerChoices: unresolved issue choices, questions: exact remaining evidence questions, commitAllowed: false }. Bind checkpoint = reconcileRecoveryCheckpoint(saved, request, serviceState, proposal). Preserve all issue histories and receipts by stable operation ID; duplicate receipt replay is a no-op, and a lost response remains unknown until matching receipt/readback evidence arrives. Return { proposal, checkpoint, operationsRequiringReadback: proposal.uncertainOperations, independentlyClosedIssueIds: issue IDs closed by exact receipts or explicit accepted alternatives } as ServiceRecoveryRun.
